*** Probe: `***` immediately followed by `(` starts a MULTILINE block comment.
***
*** Maude manual, Appendix B.3: comments are `***` or `---` to end of line,
*** and `***( ... )` is a multiline comment delimited by balanced parentheses.
*** Whitespace between `***` and `(` is accepted, so a line comment whose
*** first non-space character is `(` unexpectedly becomes a block comment that
*** ends at the matching `)`.
***
*** Consequence: in the line below the comment ends at the `)`, so `w1` is
*** tokenized and Maude reports "skipped unexpected token: w1".
*** (a) w1
fmod BLOCK-COMMENT-BAD is
  sort S .
  op a : -> S .
endfm

*** A `(` later in the line does not start a block comment, because `foo`
*** comes first, so this whole line is an ordinary line comment.
*** foo (b) w2
fmod BLOCK-COMMENT-GOOD is
  sort S .
  op a : -> S .
endfm
